\label{sec:lower-dimensional-inputs}

The following auxiliary result is used inside the moving-centre
and jet arguments. Its varieties have dimension at most two;
it does not assume threefold nef nonvanishing.

\label{lem:positive-boundary}
Suppose $\nef(X,D)=3$. If $G\ge0$ is rational, $(X,G)$ is klt,
and $\kappa(G)>0$, then $G+cD$ is big for every rational $c>0$.

\label{prop:smaller-nef}
If $\nef(X,D)<3$, then $D$ has an effective rational numerical
representative, and $H^0(X,mD)\ne0$ for some $m>0$.
